hadiths[68]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1720","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan and Shu'bah, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from al-Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said:\n\nA man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, seeking his permission to engage in jihad. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, asked: \Do you have parents?\"" The man replied: \""Yes.\"" The Prophet"
"1721","Narrated As-Sa'ib bin Yazid: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arrived from Tabuk"""
"1722","Narrated 'Umar bin Al-Khattab: \The wealth of Banu An-Nadir was among the spoils of war which Allah granted upon His Messenger (ﷺ) which the Muslims did not gain with the rush of their horses nor camel. So it was purely for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"1723","Narrated Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Wearing silk and gold has made unlawful for the males of my Ummah and lawful for its females. [Abu 'Eisa said:] There are narrations on this topic from 'Umar"""
"1724","Narrated Suwaid bin Ghafalah: That 'Umar gave a Khutbah at Al-Jabiyah and he said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited silk except for two finger's worth of space"""
"1725","Narrated Anas bin Malik: That 'Abdur Rahman bin 'Awf and Az-Zubair bin Al-'Awwam complained of lice to the Prophet (ﷺ) during a battle that they participated in. So he permitted them to wear silk shirts. He (Anas) said: \I saw them wearing them.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"""
"1726","Narrated Waqid bin 'Amr bin Sa'd bin Mu'adh: \Anas bin Malik arrived. So I went to him and he said: 'Who are you ?' I said: 'I am Waqid bin 'Amr [bin Sa'd bin Ma'adh].'\"" He said: \""So he began to cry and he said: 'You resemble Sa'd. Sa'd was one of the greatest people"""
"1727","Narrated Al-Bara' : \I have not seen anyone with hair past his shoulders in a red Hullah more handsome than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He had hair that would flow on his shoulders"""
"1728","Narrated 'Ali: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited wearing Al-Qassi and what was dyed with 'Usfur.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] There are narrations on this topic from Anas and 'Abdullah bin 'Amr"""
"1729","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Ukaim: ""A letter came from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'Do not use the skins of dead animals, nor tendons.'"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan. This Hadith has been related to 'Abdullah bin 'Ukaim from some Shuyukh of his, and this is not acted upon according to most of the people of knowledge. And this Hadith has been related from 'Abdullah bin 'Ukaim, that he said: ""A letter came to us from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) two months before he died."" He said: I heart Ahmad bin Al-Hasan saying: ""Ahmad bin Hanbal followed this Hadith due to it mentioning that it was two months before he (ﷺ) died. Then Ahmad left this Hadith because of their Idtirab in its chain, since some of them reported it, saying: 'From 'Abdullah bin 'Ukaim from some Shuyukh of his from Juhainah"
"1730","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: \A sheep died so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to its owners: 'Why dont you remove its skin"""
"1731","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Any skin tanned"""
"1732","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Ukaim: \A letter came from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'Do not use the skins of dead animals"""
"1733","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Umar: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \On the day of judgement"""
"1734","Narrated Ibn 'Umar: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever arrogantly drags his garment"""
"1735","Narrated Umm Salamah: \The Prophet (ﷺ) slackened Fatimah's garment a hand-span.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] Some of them reported it from Hammad bin Salamah"""
"1736","Narrated Abu Burdah: \'Aishah brought a patched woolen Kisa' (cloak)"""
"1737","Narrated Ibn Mas'ud: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \On the day of His Lord spoke to him"""
"1738","Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī al-Muqaddamī al-Baṣrī narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Sufyān ibn Ḥusayn, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \I indeed saw us on the day of Ḥunayn"
"1739","Narrated Nafi': That Ibn 'Umar said: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would wear an 'Imamah would hang between his shoulders.\"" Nafi' said: \""Ibn 'Umar would hang his 'Imamah between his shoulders.\"" 'Ubaidullah said: \""And I saw Al-Qasim and Salim doing that.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Gharib. And there is something on this topic from 'Ali. And this Hadith of 'Ali about this is not correct due to its chain"""
"1740","Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited me from rings of gold"""
"1741","Narrated 'Imran bin Husain: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited us from (wearing) rings of gold.\"" [He said:] THere are narrations on this topic from 'Ali"""
"1742","Narrated Anas: \The Prophet (ﷺ) had ring made of silver and its stone (Fass) was Ethiopian.\"" He said: There are narrations on this topic from Ibn 'Umar and Buraidah. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih Gharib from this route"""
"1743","Narrated Anas: \The ring of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was made of silver"""
"1744","Narrated Ibn 'Umar: \The Prophet (ﷺ) had a ring of gold made for him which he wore on his right (hand). Then he sat on the Minbar and said: 'I did indeed have this ring on my right hand' then he discarded it and the people discarded their rings.\"" He said: There are narrations on this topic from 'Ali"""
"1745","Narrated As-Salt bin 'Abdullah bin Nawfal: \Ibn Abbas wore a ring on his right hand. And I do not doubt he said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wearing a ring on his right hand.'\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] Muhammad bin Isma'il said: \""The Hadith is Muhammad bin Ishaq from As-Salt bin 'Abdullah bin Nawfal is a Hasan Sahih Hadith"""
"1746","Narrated Ja'far bin Muhammad : Narrated from his father who said: \Al-Hasan and Al-Husain wore their ring on their left hand.\"" This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"""
"1747","Narrated Hammad bin Salamah: \I saw Ibn Rafi' [and he is 'Ubaidullah bin Abi Rafi'"""
"1748","Narrated Anas bin Malik: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had a ring made from silver"""
"1749","Narrated Anas: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered the area in which he would relieve himself"""
"1750","Narrated Anas bin Malik:\The inscription on the ring of the Prophet (ﷺ) was in three lines: 'Muhammad' on a line"""
"1751","Narrated Anas bin Malik: \The inscription on the ring of the Prophet (ﷺ) was in three line: 'Muhammad' on a line"""
"1752","Narrated Jabir: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited having images in the house"""
"1753","Narrated Abu Dharr: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed the best of what the gray may be changed with is Henna' and Katam."" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. Abu Al-Aswad Ad-Dili's (a narrator in this chain) name is Zalim bin 'Amr bin Sufyan"
"1754","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever fashions an image"""
"1755","Narrated 'Aishah: ""I and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would perform Ghusl using (water from) the same vessel. He had hair reaching above his shoulders and below his earlobes."" This Hadith is Hasan Sahih Gharib. [Abu 'Eisa said:] It has been reported from other routes that 'Aishah said: ""I and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would perform Ghusl using (water from) the same vessel."" And the following statement is not mentioned in it: ""He had hair reaching above his shoulders [and below his earlobes'."" It was only mentioned by 'Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Az-Zinad, and he is trustworthy, a Hafiz, and Malik bin Anas stated that he was trustworthy and ordered recording (Ahadith) from him"
"1756","Narrated Abu Dharr: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Indeed the best of what the gray may be changed with is Henna' and Katam.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. Abu Al-Aswad Ad-Dili's (a narrator in this chain) name is Zalim bin 'Amr bin Sufyan"""
"1757","Narrated Anas: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was of average height"""
"1758","Narrated 'Aishah: \I and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would perform Ghusl using (water from) the same vessel. He had hair reaching above his shoulders and below his earlobes.\"" This Hadith is Hasan Sahih Gharib. [Abu 'Eisa said:] It has been reported from other routes that 'Aishah said: \""I and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would perform Ghusl using (water from) the same vessel.\"" And the following statement is not mentioned in it: \""He had hair reaching above his shoulders [and below his earlobes'.\"" It was only mentioned by 'Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Az-Zinad"""
"1759","Narrated Abu Hurairah: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited two types of dress: As-Sama'"""
"1760","Narrated Ibn 'Umar: That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Allah has cursed the woman who artificially lengthens and the woman who seeks to have her hair artificially lengthened"""
"1761","Narrated Al-Bara' bin 'Azib: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited riding (while sitting on) Miyathir.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] There are narrations on this topic from 'Ali and Mu'awiyah. The Hadith if Al-Bara' is Hasan Sahih. Shu'bah reported similarly from Ash'ath bin Abi Ash-Sha'tha' in the lengthy Hadith"""
"1762","Narrated 'Aishah: \The only bed that the Messenger of Allah had which he slept was [made of a tanned skin] stuffed with palm-fibres.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. He Said: There are narrations on thus topic from Hafsah and Jabir"""
"1763","Narrated Umm Salamah: \The most loved garment to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was the Qamis (long shirt).\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Gharib. We only know of it as a narration of 'Abdul-Mu'min bin Khalid (a narrator in the chain of this Hadith) who was alone in narrating it"""
"1764","Narrated Umm Salamah:\The most loved garment to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was the Qamis (long shirt)"""
"1765","Narrated Umm Salamah:\The most loved garment to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was the Qamis (long shirt)"""
"1766","Narrated Asma' bint Yazid bin As-Sakan Al-Ansariyyah:\The sleeves of (the shirt) of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) were to the wrist.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Gharib"""
"1767","Narrated Abu Hurairah: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) put on a Qamis he began with the right side. [Abu 'Eisa said:] Others have reported this Hadith from Shu'bah with this chain"""
"1768","Narrated 'Urwah bin Al-Mugirah bin Shu'bah: From his father: \The Prophet (ﷺ) wore a Roman Jubbah with tight sleeves.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"""
"1769","Narrated Ash-Sha'bi: From Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah: \Dihyah Al-Kalbi gave a pair of Khuff to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"1770","Narrated Abu Al-Malih:\The Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited predator skins.\"" And this chain is more correct"""
"1771","Ibn Abi 'Umar narrated to us: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Shihab, from Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadithan, who said: I heard 'Umar ibn al-Khattab say: The wealth of Banu al-Nadir was part of what Allah bestowed upon His Messenger without the Muslims having to ride horses or camels to obtain it. It belonged exclusively to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He would set aside provisions for his family for one year, and then place the remainder in weapons and equipment as preparation for the cause of Allah. Abu 'Isa said: This is a hasan sahih hadith. Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah also narrated this hadith from Ma'mar, from Ibn Shihab."
"1772","Narrated 'Urwah bin Al-Mugirah bin Shu'bah: From his father: \The Prophet (ﷺ) wore a Roman Jubbah with tight sleeves.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"""
"1773","Narrated Ash-Sha'bi: From Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah: \Dihyah Al-Kalbi gave a pair of Khuff to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""
"1774","# Hadith Translation\n\n**Narrated by Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased him):**\n\nAbdur-Rahman ibn Awf and Az-Zubayr ibn Al-Awwam (may Allah be pleased with them both) complained to the Prophet ﷺ of lice infestation during one of their military expeditions. He ﷺ granted them permission to wear shirts of silk. He (Anas) said: \And I saw them wearing them.\""\n\n**Abu Isa (At-Tirmidhi) said:** This is a *hasan sahih* (good and authentic) hadith.\n\n---\n\n## Chain of Narration (Isnād)\n\nMahmūd ibn Ghaylān narrated to us"
"1775","we only know of it as a narration of 'Abdur-Rahman bin Tarafah. Salm bin Zarir reported similar to the narration of Abu Al-Ashhab from 'Abdur-Rahman bin Taraqah - from 'Abdur-Rahman bin Taraqah. It has been related about more than one of the people of knowledge that they would brace their teeth with gold, and in this Hadith there was a proof for them.\\n"
"1776","Zarir is more correct, and Abu Sa'd As-San'ani's (a narrator in this chain) name is Muhammad bin Muyassir. \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 1770 Arabic Hadees: 1770\""1777"""
"1777","Qutaybah narrated to us: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us from Nafi', from Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from his father, from 'Ali, who said: The Prophet ﷺ forbade me from wearing al-qassi and al-mu'asfar. Abu 'Isa said: And in this chapter there are narrations from Anas and 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr. And the hadith of 'Ali is hasan sahih."
"1778","Narrated Qatadah:\I asked Anas bin Malik: 'How were the sandals of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ? He said: 'They had two straps"""
"1779","Narrated Qatadah: From Anas: \The sandals of the Prophet (ﷺ) had two straps.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. He said: There are narrations on this topic from Ibn 'Abbas"""
"1780","Narrated Abu Hurairah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not walk in one sandal"""
"1781","Narrated Abu Hurairah: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited that a man should put on sandals while he is standing.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Gharib. 'Ubaidullah bin 'Amr Ar-Raqqi reported this Hadith from Ma'mar"""
"1782","Narrated Anas: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited that a man should put on sandals while he is standing.\"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Gharib. Muhammad bin Isma'il said: \""This Hadith is not correct"""
"1783","Narrated 'Aishah:\Sometimes the Prophet (ﷺ) would walk in one sandal"""
"1784","# Translation of the Hadith\n\n**Narrated by Ishaq ibn Mansur:** Affan informed us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Umm al-Hasan al-Basriyyah, that Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated to them that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) measured for Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) a hand-span (*shibr*) from her waist-wrapper (*nitaq*).\n\nAbu Isa [al-Tirmidhi] said: And some of them narrated from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her).\n\nAbu Isa further commented: **In this Hadith there is a dispensation (*rukhsah*) for women regarding dragging the lower garment (*izār*), for it provides greater concealment (*satr*) for them.**\n\n---\n\n### Scholarly Notes:\n\n- **"
"1785","Narrated Abu Hurairah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When one of you dons sandals"""
"1786","Narrated 'Aishah: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: 'If you want to stick with me"""
"1787","# Hadith Translation\n\n**Narrated by Jābin (may Allāh be pleased with him):**\n\nMuḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us, from Ḥammād ibn Salamah, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:\n\n**\The Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) entered Makkah on the Day of the Conquest wearing a black turban (ʿimāmah).\""**\n\nHe (the narrator) said: **\""In this chapter (bāb)"
